## Locked pages are locked — no exceptions without confirmation

"Locked" means **no changes of any kind** — not text, images, diagrams, stats, structure, **and not color, styling, spacing, layout, or CSS either.** That covers edits to the HTML, inline `style` attributes, scoped `<style>` blocks, **and the shared stylesheet files** (`sales-document.css`, `capabilities-document.css`, `brochure.css`, `scope-of-work.css`, `budgetary-estimate.css`).

### Pre-edit gate — run before every edit

Before making any edit, check the target element/selector against the template `SKILL.md` editable-regions list:

- **Target listed as editable** → proceed.
- **Target NOT listed as editable, or IS in a locked list** → **do NOT edit.** Stop and tell the user:

  > "Page X is locked per the `<template>` SKILL.md. Do you want to override that? And if so, should it be **local to this client doc only** or **canonical** (master + shared CSS, propagates to all docs)?"

  Wait for the answer before editing.

A user request to change a locked page is **not** an override by itself — it is the trigger for this pause-and-confirm. Never edit a locked page first and mention it after.

## All details live in _brand/SKILL.md

The full workflow, efficient customization rules, fit check, page packing, voice, PDF export, and open-preview instructions are all in `_brand/SKILL.md`. Read it once and follow it. Do not re-read it every turn — it doesn't change mid-conversation.
